  "english": "Seventh Psalm 101 [102], say in full: \"I became like an owl in the ruins\" (Eghē es vorpēs bu yaveraki). Variant: \"Lord, hear my prayer, and let my cry\" (Tēr lur aghōt’its imots aghaghak im).\nProphet Jeremiah 11:18: \"The Lord made it known to me...\" to 12:8: \"...therefore I hated her.\"\nApostle Hebrews 10:19: \"Therefore, brethren, having...\" to verse 31: \"...of the living God.\"\nSong: \"By Speaking\" (Barbarelov).\nGospel Luke 22:66: \"And as soon as it was day...\" to 23:49: \"...beholding these things.\"\n\nEighth Psalm 142 [143], say in full: \"My soul thirsts for you like a parched land\" (Andzn im vorpēs erkir). Variant: \"Lord, hear my prayer\" (Tēr lur aghōt’its imots).\nProphet Zechariah 14:5: \"And the Lord shall come...\" to verse 11: \"...Jerusalem shall dwell in hope.\"\nApostle 1 Timothy 6:13: \"I urge you...\" to verse 16: \"...forever. Amen.\"\nSong: \"Of the Fountains\" (Aghberatsn).\nGospel John 19:17: \"And he bearing his cross...\" to verse 37: \"...whom they pierced.\"\nAnd then, hymn [sharakán] Tone 2 [b-g/bk]: \"Your Cross, O Christ\" (Khach’i k’o K’ristos), according to the above canon; but here: \"We magnify Your holy sufferings, and we glorify Your holy crucifixion,\" and the rest in order.\nLikewise: \"Glory to Your holy cross, alleluia; to Your sufferings, alleluia; to Your crucifixion, alleluia,\" and the rest as set down above.\nThen, hymn [sharakán] Tone 2 [b-g/bk]: \"The Life-Giving Cross\" (Khach’n kenarar).\nAfterward, Litany: \"By this holy Cross\" (Surb khach’ivs). Prayer: \"Protect us\" (Pahpanea).\nAnd they shall kiss the holy Cross and the Gospel, and be dismissed.\n\nBut at the tenth hour, having assembled in the church, they shall perform the Order of the Burial of Christ God.\nBut first: \"Bow down Your ear\" (Khonarhēts’o) and \"Deliver me\" (Aprets’o). \"Gladsome Light\" (Luys zuart’).\nGradual [Mesedi]: \"They gave me gall for my food.\" Variant: \"Let their table be...\"\nProphet Jeremiah 11:18: \"The Lord made it known to me...\" to 12:8: \"...I hated her.\"\nProphet Isaiah 52:13: \"Behold, my servant shall understand...\" to 53:12: \"...he was delivered.\"\nPsalm 21 [22], say in full: \"They divided...\" Variant: \"My God, my God\" (Astuats astuats im).\nAnd then: \"Let my prayer be set forth.\" Litany: \"Let us entreat.\"\n\"Holy God,\" who wast crucified.\nBut the priests and the people shall fall on their knees; but they shall not say \"Glorified\" (P’araworealn).\nHymn of the Evening [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [d-k/gk], stēghi [melody type]: \"Come, believers\" (Ekayk’ hawatats’ealk’).\nAfter \"Compassionate Father\" (Hayr gt’atsin), Psalm...",
